{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/39", "id": 5112584457, "node_id": "PR_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABMLvZCQ", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/39", "diff_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/39.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/39.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/39", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/39/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/39/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/39/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/statuses/064aa9efcd7ca1d6b5eaa2d4995c7df0b768d359", "number": 39, "state": "open", "locked": false, "title": "Add the native Ginux controller desktop", "user": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "## Summary\n\nThis adds a native graphical controller environment to Ginux without turning\nthe controller into a Linux desktop or adopting Wayland as the host display\nserver.\n\nGinux owns the physical display and input seat, renders a trusted controller\nshell in ring 3, and can present Linux domain desktops as bounded, revocable\nsurfaces. The serial controller remains an independent recovery path.\n\n## Final controller GUI\n\n![Ginux controller desktop](https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/blob/064aa9efcd7ca1d6b5eaa2d4995c7df0b768d359/docs/images/controller-desktop-final.png?raw=1)\n\n## Completed HDAE gates\n\n- **19 — Architecture:** established the controller trust boundary, native\n  compositor model, seats, focus, leases, domain surfaces, and recovery rules.\n- **20 — Graphical runtime:** added the ring-3 graphical service lifecycle and\n  preserved serial recovery.\n- **21 — Display and input:** added framebuffer, keyboard, and pointer support\n  with bounded kernel/controller interfaces.\n- **22 — Display protocol:** added a versioned, capability-scoped native surface\n  protocol with validated buffers and damage.\n- **23 — Seats and leases:** added explicit focus, input routing, revocation,\n  ownership, and generation-safe recovery.\n- **24 — Windowing:** added the native software compositor, window model,\n  controls, and toolkit primitives.\n- **25 — Controller application:** added graphical system management backed by\n  the same live kernel state as the CLI.\n- **26 — Domain bridge:** added virtual display and input transport for domains.\n- **27 — Linux/Wayland:** added the minimal domain-side Wayland environment and\n  exported desktop surface.\n- **28 — Presentation:** added managed windowed and full-screen domain desktop\n  presentation.\n- **29 — Recovery:** hardened crash, disconnect, stop, timeout, focus, lease,\n  and buffer cleanup paths.\n- **30 — Qualification:** added deterministic QEMU integration, stress,\n  performance, isolation, and recovery coverage.\n- **31 — Visual design:** delivered the accepted native 1024×768 controller\n  shell with antialiased Inter typography, compact layout, live data, responsive\n  mouse input, clickable navigation, and a confirmation-safe power menu.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make test-controller-desktop-all` — complete protocol, windowing,\n  controller, domain display, Wayland, presentation, recovery, boot, visible\n  framebuffer, and 2-vCPU/4-vCPU stress coverage passed.\n- `make test-controller-desktop-latency` — 20.844 ms visible-frame p95,\n  20.973 ms maximum, and 20.485 ms complete page presentation.\n- `make test-controller-desktop-performance` — 835 µs input-to-frame p95,\n  863 µs steady-frame p95, and a bounded 3,175,728-byte modeled working set.\n- `make check` — architecture, unsafe baseline, ABI, formatting, lint, unit,\n  and compatibility checks passed.\n\n## Current boundaries\n\n- Software rendering only; GPU acceleration and DRM/KMS compatibility remain\n  outside this iteration.\n- Linux domains export one composed desktop surface rather than individual\n  application windows.\n- The CLI remains available as the recovery and low-level management path.\n", "labels": [], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2026-11-01T23:18:47Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-01T23:18:47Z", "closed_at": null, "merged_at": null, "merge_commit_sha": null, "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "gmkurtzer:codex/controller-desktop", "ref": "codex/controller-desktop", "repo": {"id": 1413787216, "node_id": "R_kgDOVESuUA", "name": "ginux", "full_name": "gmkurtzer/ginux", "owner": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gm